  },
  "Solution": {
    "S": "Using the Arrhenius equation in logarithmic form:\n\n$$\\log_{10} \\frac{k_2}{k_1} = \\frac{E_a}{2.303R} \\left( \\frac{T_2 - T_1}{T_1 T_2} \\right)$$\n\nGiven: $k_2 = 0.58$, $k_1 = 0.026$, $T_2 = 300$ K, $T_1 = 290$ K, $R = 8.314$ J K⁻¹ mol⁻¹.\n\n$$\\log_{10} \\frac{0.58}{0.026} = \\log_{10} (22.3077) = 1.3484$$\n\n$$\\frac{T_2 - T_1}{T_1 T_2} = \\frac{10}{290 \\times 300} = 1.1494 \\times 10^{-4}$$\n\n$$2.303R = 2.303 \\times 8.314 = 19.15$$\n\nSubstituting:\n\n$$1.3484 = \\frac{E_a}{19.15} \\times 1.1494 \\times 10^{-4}$$\n\n$$E_a = \\frac{1.3484 \\times 19.15}{1.1494 \\times 10^{-4}} = \\frac{25.82}{1.1494 \\times 10^{-4}} = 224538 \\text{ J/mol} = 224.54 \\text{ kJ/mol}$$\n\nThus the correct option is B: 224.55 kJ."
  },
